<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shakya Zangpo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1270</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shakya Zangpo was the first ponchen, or civil administrator, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> under the Sakya regime, appointed with the backing of the Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>. While the Sakya lama Phagpa spent much time at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>, Shakya Zangpo governed from Sakya monastery, organised the Tibetan districts for Mongol administration and began building the great Lhakhang Chenmo temple there.</p></div>
